(2501819, 343603, 24073, '<td valign="top">I so very much wanted to give this a 10.  The problem that I am seeing is with her eyes.  It doesn''t seem to me that her eyes are totally in focus, just a tad bit blurry.  And beings her eyes are one of the main focal points, if not the main focal point, it really takes away from the photo.  As for the rest of the photo, it is amazing.<br/>   I know Librodo is a master of these shots, so if you were having trouble with working out that blurriness in the center, he''d be the one to ask, I''m sure he wouldn''t hesitate in answering, especially with a photo of this caliber.  GL, I hope this does well.</td>', 'I so very much wanted to give this a 10.  The problem that I am seeing is with her eyes.  It doesn''t seem to me that her eyes are totally in focus, just a tad bit blurry.  And beings her eyes are one of the main focal points, if not the main focal point, it really takes away from the photo.  As for the rest of the photo, it is amazing.   I know Librodo is a master of these shots, so if you were having trouble with working out that blurriness in the center, he''d be the one to ask, I''m sure he wouldn''t hesitate in answering, especially with a photo of this caliber.  GL, I hope this does well.', '2006-06-09 10:49:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2501824, 344408, 24073, '<td valign="top">The simplicity you used here really works for me, I like that part very much.  I''m not for sure that the subject matter is interesting enough to break that extrodinary mark.  GL.</td>', 'The simplicity you used here really works for me, I like that part very much.  I''m not for sure that the subject matter is interesting enough to break that extrodinary mark.  GL.', '2006-06-09 10:51:24.000000', NULL, 1),
