(2515920, 344285, 50695, '<td valign="top">I was disheartened by all the comments not liking the green blades across his face. For me, that was the raison d''etre of the image. And now I''m surprised that the avg score among commentors is so high!</td>', 'I was disheartened by all the comments not liking the green blades across his face. For me, that was the raison d''etre of the image. And now I''m surprised that the avg score among commentors is so high!', '2006-06-14 09:51:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2515942, 343187, 47909, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for their comments and appreciation of this photo.  I am thrilled with my first ribbon here.  I was doing some photography work for a local golf course and decided to take my clubs and son (Ben - 3 yrs old) along with me.  After taking enough photos of the course I decided to take a few practice golf shots.  Ben looked cute on the green so I loaded him up with what I knew would be too many balls to hang on to and grabbed my camera.  He didn''t even know I was taking photos of him.  I got a lot of nice shots from that day.<br/> <br/>Steps:<br/>Remove Noise<br/>High Pass Sharpen<br/>Resized to 1500<br/>Changed Hue<br/>Curves<br/>Resized to 640<br/>Sharpend<br/> <br/>No cropping or rotating.<br/> <br/>Thanks Again,<br/>Brian<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks to everyone for their comments and appreciation of this photo.  I am thrilled with my first ribbon here.  I was doing some photography work for a local golf course and decided to take my clubs and son (Ben - 3 yrs old) along with me.  After taking enough photos of the course I decided to take a few practice golf shots.  Ben looked cute on the green so I loaded him up with what I knew would be too many balls to hang on to and grabbed my camera.  He didn''t even know I was taking photos of him.  I got a lot of nice shots from that day. Steps:Remove NoiseHigh Pass SharpenResized to 1500Changed HueCurvesResized to 640Sharpend No cropping or rotating. Thanks Again,Brian ', '2006-06-14 09:57:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2515947, 344412, 25678, '<td valign="top">What a shot!  Congratulations on another ribbon!  Maybe we should start calling you the reptile/amphibian girl!</td>', 'What a shot!  Congratulations on another ribbon!  Maybe we should start calling you the reptile/amphibian girl!', '2006-06-14 10:02:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2515958, 344432, 55697, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who voted on or even just viewed my submission.  I really learn a great deal from other peoples pictures and comments. The picture did better than I had hoped, so I''m very happy. Thanks again and I''m looking forward to more "learning experiences".</td>', 'Thanks to everyone who voted on or even just viewed my submission.  I really learn a great deal from other peoples pictures and comments. The picture did better than I had hoped, so I''m very happy. Thanks again and I''m looking forward to more "learning experiences".', '2006-06-14 10:09:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2516022, 341348, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment <br/> <br/>Composition/subject - Great choice of subject!  Composition is good to get the body on the diagonal and get the wings nicely in the frame without being cramped.  The picture would be better without the stick on the right and a bit less clutter in the background but when shooting nature, you take what you get!<br/> <br/>Technical - Really very smooth given that it was shot at 1600!  Focus is excellent.<br/> <br/>Meets challenge - Yep, there''s green in it.  Like the bits of green in the background, too.<br/> <br/>My opinion - A good bug shot, fascinating to look at.  Not sure why it didn''t score higher, but the sixes outnumbered the fours which is good.</td>', 'Trading Post comment  Composition/subject - Great choice of subject!  Composition is good to get the body on the diagonal and get the wings nicely in the frame without being cramped.  The picture would be better without the stick on the right and a bit less clutter in the background but when shooting nature, you take what you get! Technical - Really very smooth given that it was shot at 1600!  Focus is excellent. Meets challenge - Yep, there''s green in it.  Like the bits of green in the background, too. My opinion - A good bug shot, fascinating to look at.  Not sure why it didn''t score higher, but the sixes outnumbered the fours which is good.', '2006-06-14 10:27:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2516024, 344412, 48456, '<td valign="top">HAHAHA this is so cute<br/>congrats on the original and clever photo!!!</td>', 'HAHAHA this is so cutecongrats on the original and clever photo!!!', '2006-06-14 10:28:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2516037, 342680, 14620, '<td valign="top">Beautiful Ron! :)</td>', 'Beautiful Ron! :)', '2006-06-14 10:29:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2516069, 343734, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment <br/> <br/>Composition/subject - I really like these pictures where the subject is camoflauged so I like your subject choice.  I''d almost like the shot better with the top cropped a bit more, leaving the eye just below the center line, but that''s just me.<br/> <br/>Technical -  Good use of depth of field, very good exposure and post processing to get such detail and clarity in a monochromatic shot.  Only nit is the OOF background seems to command a bit more attention that it should due to the highlights.  Not sure if a bit of burning would help (though not permitted for this challenge, of course.)<br/> <br/>Meets challenge - Yep.<br/> <br/>My opinion - I like it.</td>', 'Trading Post comment  Composition/subject - I really like these pictures where the subject is camoflauged so I like your subject choice.  I''d almost like the shot better with the top cropped a bit more, leaving the eye just below the center line, but that''s just me. Technical -  Good use of depth of field, very good exposure and post processing to get such detail and clarity in a monochromatic shot.  Only nit is the OOF background seems to command a bit more attention that it should due to the highlights.  Not sure if a bit of burning would help (though not permitted for this challenge, of course.) Meets challenge - Yep. My opinion - I like it.', '2006-06-14 10:34:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2516097, 343839, 42135, '<td valign="top">Beautiful work!! Congrats on your top 20 finish!! :)</td>', 'Beautiful work!! Congrats on your top 20 finish!! :)', '2006-06-14 10:38:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2516109, 344490, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment <br/> <br/>Composition/subject - I wonder how many people "got" the title.  The choice of subject is appropriate for the challenge (though I suspect some probably got tired of this subject while voting).  Composition is more interesting than the normal "leaf" shot, though I can see moving the seam between the two leafs further left a bit.<br/> <br/>Technical - Depth of field works for me.  Lighting is a bit flat, but sufficient for this shot.<br/> <br/>Meets challenge - It''s green so it''s a fair bet this meets the challenge. <br/> <br/>My opinion - I think this would make an interesting series.</td>', 'Trading Post comment  Composition/subject - I wonder how many people "got" the title.  The choice of subject is appropriate for the challenge (though I suspect some probably got tired of this subject while voting).  Composition is more interesting than the normal "leaf" shot, though I can see moving the seam between the two leafs further left a bit. Technical - Depth of field works for me.  Lighting is a bit flat, but sufficient for this shot. Meets challenge - It''s green so it''s a fair bet this meets the challenge.  My opinion - I think this would make an interesting series.', '2006-06-14 10:40:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2516120, 344404, 42135, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!! Congrats on your top 20 finish!!</td>', 'Beautiful!! Congrats on your top 20 finish!!', '2006-06-14 10:42:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2516147, 342960, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment <br/> <br/>Composition/subject - I didn''t vote in this challenge and truthfully never got a chance to even look through the entries, but I suspected you might have used Kermit... I really like Kermit so I''m down with the subject choice.  :-)  Good environment in which to stick Kermie.  Only nit on the composition is lay of the fishing line - I''d have preferred it straight out to the point where the float is. <br/> <br/>Technical - Good exposure, good color, good contrast.  All good. <br/> <br/>Meets challenge - Yep<br/> <br/>My opinion - Nice use of a good prop.  As I mentioned, the only thing I don''t like is the way the fishing line is angled.  (So are 6s getting boring now?)  Heh - just noticed that Kermie is in 3 of your top 6!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-14 09:51:19.</i></td>', 'Trading Post comment  Composition/subject - I didn''t vote in this challenge and truthfully never got a chance to even look through the entries, but I suspected you might have used Kermit... I really like Kermit so I''m down with the subject choice.  :-)  Good environment in which to stick Kermie.  Only nit on the composition is lay of the fishing line - I''d have preferred it straight out to the point where the float is.  Technical - Good exposure, good color, good contrast.  All good.  Meets challenge - Yep My opinion - Nice use of a good prop.  As I mentioned, the only thing I don''t like is the way the fishing line is angled.  (So are 6s getting boring now?)  Heh - just noticed that Kermie is in 3 of your top 6!', '2006-06-14 10:49:34.000000', '2006-06-14 10:51:19.000000', 0),
(2516198, 341303, 30982, '<td valign="top">Great portrait!  I''m sure the subject''s family is suitably impressed and hope you gave them a copy for their den.  :-)  Seriously, this is an awesome shot - great "pose" and composition, and definitely green.  And I gotta differ with some commenters - I think the subject is very cute in this capture!</td>', 'Great portrait!  I''m sure the subject''s family is suitably impressed and hope you gave them a copy for their den.  :-)  Seriously, this is an awesome shot - great "pose" and composition, and definitely green.  And I gotta differ with some commenters - I think the subject is very cute in this capture!', '2006-06-14 11:01:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2516277, 344394, 39632, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.  The blurriness is not a lack of focus, it''s motion blur.  I took this around 10pm at night in my kitchen, and there just wasn''t enough ambient light to get fast enough shutter speeds to freeze the action.  I plan on re-taking this shot in natural light to try and improve upon it.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments.  The blurriness is not a lack of focus, it''s motion blur.  I took this around 10pm at night in my kitchen, and there just wasn''t enough ambient light to get fast enough shutter speeds to freeze the action.  I plan on re-taking this shot in natural light to try and improve upon it.', '2006-06-14 11:22:03.000000', NULL, 0),
