(2519150, 344068, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ralfw:</b></div><hr/><i> Ah, IreneM -<br/>I sensed this might be one of your new experiments!  I like it!<br/> <br/>You''ve inspired me to start working with splashes and drops by the way.  My wife told me to take it outside, and to stop making so much of a mess!<br/> <br/>Great timing on that capture.  Do you normally use a laser to trigger the exposure, or just hand time it and pick from the best?<br/> <br/>ralfw </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Ralf, I''ve sent you a PM.</td>', 'Originally posted by ralfw: Ah, IreneM -I sensed this might be one of your new experiments!  I like it! You''ve inspired me to start working with splashes and drops by the way.  My wife told me to take it outside, and to stop making so much of a mess! Great timing on that capture.  Do you normally use a laser to trigger the exposure, or just hand time it and pick from the best? ralfw   Hi Ralf, I''ve sent you a PM.', '2006-06-15 05:41:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2519790, 342250, 42125, '<td valign="top"><b>CTCP2 Gunnsi<br/>First impression:</b> <br/>Lovely looking Peacock. Yes and it is green all over.<br/><b>What can you do better?</b> <br/>IMO when shooting a bird the details in the feathers must come through. In this case you show it all but there are details missing. Maybe a closer view (more details) of its head with few green feathers in the background or in front would have scored better. Also if you had caught a female bird in front or just something that would make this picture more than just a lovely bird. <br/>I saw a good thread here on DPC yesterday:<br/>//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=156130&amp;page=3</td>', 'CTCP2 GunnsiFirst impression: Lovely looking Peacock. Yes and it is green all over.What can you do better? IMO when shooting a bird the details in the feathers must come through. In this case you show it all but there are details missing. Maybe a closer view (more details) of its head with few green feathers in the background or in front would have scored better. Also if you had caught a female bird in front or just something that would make this picture more than just a lovely bird. I saw a good thread here on DPC yesterday://www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&FORUM_THREAD_ID=156130&page=3', '2006-06-15 10:42:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2519804, 343734, 2490, '<td valign="top">==Trading Post==<br/> <br/>It''s definitely green :)  It does look like you had to manipulate it to achieve this level of green.  I like the diagonal, but the blurry "background" bothers me, pulling my eye away from the gator.</td>', '==Trading Post== It''s definitely green :)  It does look like you had to manipulate it to achieve this level of green.  I like the diagonal, but the blurry "background" bothers me, pulling my eye away from the gator.', '2006-06-15 10:52:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2519808, 342960, 2490, '<td valign="top">==Trading Post==<br/> <br/>I would have liked this better if Kermit had been in tan grass instead of so much green.  He''s not hard to find, but some color contrast would have really made him "pop".  <br/> <br/>Love the Kermits :)</td>', '==Trading Post== I would have liked this better if Kermit had been in tan grass instead of so much green.  He''s not hard to find, but some color contrast would have really made him "pop".   Love the Kermits :)', '2006-06-15 10:53:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2519831, 341348, 2490, '<td valign="top">==Trading Post==<br/> <br/>This is a good "opportunity" shot, and I like the blurred background.  It is a bit of a problem, though, that the background color is SO similar to the dragonfly coloring.  Makes for a lot of green, which is good for the challenge, but takes away from the impact due to the loss of "color contrast."<br/> <br/>Keep shooting!</td>', '==Trading Post== This is a good "opportunity" shot, and I like the blurred background.  It is a bit of a problem, though, that the background color is SO similar to the dragonfly coloring.  Makes for a lot of green, which is good for the challenge, but takes away from the impact due to the loss of "color contrast." Keep shooting!', '2006-06-15 11:03:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2519845, 341674, 42125, '<td valign="top"><b>CTCP2 Gunnsi<br/>First impression:</b> <br/>Great photo. I would love to run (jog) here too.<br/>Good angle, focus and lighting.<br/><b>What can you do better?</b> <br/>Add a bit contrast is the only thing that think could make this better.<br/>IMO Much to low score for this picture.</td>', 'CTCP2 GunnsiFirst impression: Great photo. I would love to run (jog) here too.Good angle, focus and lighting.What can you do better? Add a bit contrast is the only thing that think could make this better.IMO Much to low score for this picture.', '2006-06-15 11:10:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2519955, 343554, 38800, '<td valign="top">I am one of those red/green colorblind photographers you are speaking of, so I found this pretty comical. I found out I was colorblind as a child when I thought the grass was red :) Anyways, on a side note, the military often look for colorblind folk to be snipers because we have the ability to pick out camouflage due to the lack of blended colours that we see. I thought that was interesting.</td>', 'I am one of those red/green colorblind photographers you are speaking of, so I found this pretty comical. I found out I was colorblind as a child when I thought the grass was red :) Anyways, on a side note, the military often look for colorblind folk to be snipers because we have the ability to pick out camouflage due to the lack of blended colours that we see. I thought that was interesting.', '2006-06-15 12:04:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2519986, 343554, 51538, '<td valign="top">I was a non-voter on this image (rather than a 1 voter).  Not sure which is better now I have read your genuine and interesting account (and nephoto''s below).  That just goes to show that I should learn to give the benefit of the doubt... ;-)</td>', 'I was a non-voter on this image (rather than a 1 voter).  Not sure which is better now I have read your genuine and interesting account (and nephoto''s below).  That just goes to show that I should learn to give the benefit of the doubt... ;-)', '2006-06-15 12:17:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2520104, 341702, 34659, '<td valign="top">I like the idea you were going for here, but I think the lighting actually hurt your score more than anything (that and the fact that this type of subject matter usually doesn''t garner the highest marks).  The flash? highlights behind her head are distracting, as are the highlights on her face - they don''t seem to "match" the mood of the rest of the shot.  When you''re going for something this far removed from the mainstream on DPC, you''ve really got to nail the technical aspects of the shot in order to get a decent score - at least that''s my experience.  (And trust me, I''ve had more than my fair share of the LOW end of the results of that experimentation!  LOL)<br/> <br/>Things that I think work in this shot are the tilted angle, the blank stare, and the color tone choices.  Again, I believe the flash killed ya here - otherwise I think you would have gotten a pretty good score.  It garnered a 5 from me as is.  :-)  Keep at it and keep those creative juices flowing.  You''ll get there!</td>', 'I like the idea you were going for here, but I think the lighting actually hurt your score more than anything (that and the fact that this type of subject matter usually doesn''t garner the highest marks).  The flash? highlights behind her head are distracting, as are the highlights on her face - they don''t seem to "match" the mood of the rest of the shot.  When you''re going for something this far removed from the mainstream on DPC, you''ve really got to nail the technical aspects of the shot in order to get a decent score - at least that''s my experience.  (And trust me, I''ve had more than my fair share of the LOW end of the results of that experimentation!  LOL) Things that I think work in this shot are the tilted angle, the blank stare, and the color tone choices.  Again, I believe the flash killed ya here - otherwise I think you would have gotten a pretty good score.  It garnered a 5 from me as is.  :-)  Keep at it and keep those creative juices flowing.  You''ll get there!', '2006-06-15 13:33:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2520490, 342116, 17148, '<td valign="top">Shot very well...love the feel of the image...shame about the DQ...well done though</td>', 'Shot very well...love the feel of the image...shame about the DQ...well done though', '2006-06-15 16:41:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2520663, 344412, 50565, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your blue ribbon!Loved it so much made it my screen saver! (:</td>', 'Congratulations on your blue ribbon!Loved it so much made it my screen saver! (:', '2006-06-15 18:00:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2520698, 344400, 45148, '<td valign="top">beartiful self portait great work</td>', 'beartiful self portait great work', '2006-06-15 18:12:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2520809, 342529, 4226, '<td valign="top">** Critique Club **<br/> <br/>When I first look at the image, I am confused as what is the ''green'' you wanted to show? Is it the caterpillar or the green background ? <br/>You have a great shot of caterpillar here, but the background doesn''t go very well with it. I find the left top portion too distracting. If you could capture the subject from an angle to avoid the white background and may be able to keep the background all green, a green on green picture, that could have been great. <br/> <br/>A few things that I think can improve the existing picture is sharpening after resizing. also you could tone down some of the red in the background.<br/> <br/>Overall, a good subject choice, but background distracts the viewer.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions, please feel free to pm me.<br/> <br/>thanks,<br/>Gaurawa</td>', '** Critique Club ** When I first look at the image, I am confused as what is the ''green'' you wanted to show? Is it the caterpillar or the green background ? You have a great shot of caterpillar here, but the background doesn''t go very well with it. I find the left top portion too distracting. If you could capture the subject from an angle to avoid the white background and may be able to keep the background all green, a green on green picture, that could have been great.  A few things that I think can improve the existing picture is sharpening after resizing. also you could tone down some of the red in the background. Overall, a good subject choice, but background distracts the viewer. If you have any questions, please feel free to pm me. thanks,Gaurawa', '2006-06-15 18:36:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2521648, 344388, 14614, '<td valign="top">FYI 7 - marvelous variations in green tones - lighting is sparky</td>', 'FYI 7 - marvelous variations in green tones - lighting is sparky', '2006-06-16 00:10:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2521670, 344369, 27133, '<td valign="top">Congratulatiosn.  I hope you proposed.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-15 23:23:01.</i></td>', 'Congratulatiosn.  I hope you proposed.', '2006-06-16 00:22:29.000000', '2006-06-16 00:23:01.000000', 0),
(2521753, 342693, 31307, '<td valign="top">PSH!  We gave you ANOTHER ribbon?  Jeez.  We messed up.</td>', 'PSH!  We gave you ANOTHER ribbon?  Jeez.  We messed up.', '2006-06-16 01:21:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2521832, 343734, 42984, '<td valign="top"><b>::: Critique Club :::</b> <br/> <br/>Hi from the critique club, this is going to be fun, I hate critters, especially slimy green ones that want to eat me.<br/> <br/><b>First Impressions:</b> <br/>It''s not the sort of image you "like" very much is it.  I didn''t get wowed by it, but neither did I have a passive reaction.  The thing looks seriously creepy and threatening and that engaged me - always a good thing in a competition photograph.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>This is a great choice of subject because it is guaranteed to get a reaction from the viewer.  Even better that it''s partially hidden and therefore more menacing.  Even better, it''s green - right on Challenge :)<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The bottom left to top right position of the ''gator has created a leading line whilst the eye is almost on thirds.  The whole effect is a pretty good balance without being spectacularly captivating.  You really did the very best with the material available.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour, Lighting and focus):</b> <br/>I''m undecided about the depth of field.  At some point I like it then 5 minutes later I wonder how much more impact it would have had with a long DOF with all the algae sharp.  I''ve decided that I''m not prepared to release a statement at this time ... lol.  You nailed the challenge, it''s green.  Perhaps not brilliant green, but there''s really no doubt.<br/> <br/>I see you were running ISO200, was that intentional?  Fortunately with this subject grain would never be an issue.  You obviously had plenty of light at 1/5000th and f2.8.  I bet you played with the DOF, did the others look pretty ho hum?<br/> <br/><b>Growing the Vote:</b> <br/>It is perhaps a little golden if you''re really scrapping to get every last point in voting but it in no way doesn''t meet the Green challenge.  Its just that voting is hard and people have to look for differences that can cost a point.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>It''s a cool shot.  It got noticed.  It scored above average (of 5.5) but I''m really surprised about the 13 3''s - no way does it deserve that so I really don''t understand it.  I wish I did.<br/> <br/>Brett</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi from the critique club, this is going to be fun, I hate critters, especially slimy green ones that want to eat me. First Impressions: It''s not the sort of image you "like" very much is it.  I didn''t get wowed by it, but neither did I have a passive reaction.  The thing looks seriously creepy and threatening and that engaged me - always a good thing in a competition photograph. Subject: This is a great choice of subject because it is guaranteed to get a reaction from the viewer.  Even better that it''s partially hidden and therefore more menacing.  Even better, it''s green - right on Challenge :) Composition: The bottom left to top right position of the ''gator has created a leading line whilst the eye is almost on thirds.  The whole effect is a pretty good balance without being spectacularly captivating.  You really did the very best with the material available. Technical (Colour, Lighting and focus): I''m undecided about the depth of field.  At some point I like it then 5 minutes later I wonder how much more impact it would have had with a long DOF with all the algae sharp.  I''ve decided that I''m not prepared to release a statement at this time ... lol.  You nailed the challenge, it''s green.  Perhaps not brilliant green, but there''s really no doubt. I see you were running ISO200, was that intentional?  Fortunately with this subject grain would never be an issue.  You obviously had plenty of light at 1/5000th and f2.8.  I bet you played with the DOF, did the others look pretty ho hum? Growing the Vote: It is perhaps a little golden if you''re really scrapping to get every last point in voting but it in no way doesn''t meet the Green challenge.  Its just that voting is hard and people have to look for differences that can cost a point. Summary: It''s a cool shot.  It got noticed.  It scored above average (of 5.5) but I''m really surprised about the 13 3''s - no way does it deserve that so I really don''t understand it.  I wish I did. Brett', '2006-06-16 02:20:48.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2521916, 342756, 22970, '<td valign="top"><b>From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>OK keeping it real here! I think your photograph looks good and defiantly meet the challenge. I think the separation of the leaf and stitching back together is neat. I have not seen that before and It looks good. You focal point is good and the lighting is great. But I do have a few issues with the photograph that IMO kept it from going above 6.<br/> <br/>1. I think the DOF is a little to shallow. I would of loved to see the complete leaf and stitching in focus.<br/> <br/>2. To be honest and I maybe wrong but the lady bug looks fake. The reflection across the back is sold from one wing to the other and should be separated as the wings are.<br/> <br/>3. The straight line on the cut leaf seams to me it would of been better, compositionally, if it was on more of a tilt in relation to the photograph instead of the top ending up near center.<br/> <br/>Overall a good photograph that meet the challenge. Good light with good color along with creativity pushed your score upward. A few minor adjustments and I believe it would of ended up in the 6 club.<br/> <br/>I hope you find this critique helpful and if you have any questions feel free to contact me.<br/>regards,<br/>SDW</td>', 'From the Critique Club  OK keeping it real here! I think your photograph looks good and defiantly meet the challenge. I think the separation of the leaf and stitching back together is neat. I have not seen that before and It looks good. You focal point is good and the lighting is great. But I do have a few issues with the photograph that IMO kept it from going above 6. 1. I think the DOF is a little to shallow. I would of loved to see the complete leaf and stitching in focus. 2. To be honest and I maybe wrong but the lady bug looks fake. The reflection across the back is sold from one wing to the other and should be separated as the wings are. 3. The straight line on the cut leaf seams to me it would of been better, compositionally, if it was on more of a tilt in relation to the photograph instead of the top ending up near center. Overall a good photograph that meet the challenge. Good light with good color along with creativity pushed your score upward. A few minor adjustments and I believe it would of ended up in the 6 club. I hope you find this critique helpful and if you have any questions feel free to contact me.regards,SDW', '2006-06-16 03:44:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522081, 343371, 59501, '<td valign="top">I like this--very simple and straightforward. The tiny bit of edge beyond the turf could be cropped out, and it would really pop!<br/>Great shot!</td>', 'I like this--very simple and straightforward. The tiny bit of edge beyond the turf could be cropped out, and it would really pop!Great shot!', '2006-06-16 08:33:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522362, 344322, 42125, '<td valign="top">Hefði líklega verið betra að hafa stelpuna aðeins til hliðar, nota 1/3 regluna. Einnig að stækka/fara nær til að fá meira af græna hattinum inn á myndina.<br/>Gangi þér betur næst.</td>', 'Hefði líklega verið betra að hafa stelpuna aðeins til hliðar, nota 1/3 regluna. Einnig að stækka/fara nær til að fá meira af græna hattinum inn á myndina.Gangi þér betur næst.', '2006-06-16 11:55:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522385, 342867, 42125, '<td valign="top">This picture is a bit flat and lacks colour adjusting.<br/>I used the level function in GIMP (free editing software)<br/>I am not saying it is perfect but IMO it looks better and would probably score more.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=348414" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/42125/thumb/348414.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/42125/thumb/348414.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/42125/thumb/348414.jpg"/></a></td>', 'This picture is a bit flat and lacks colour adjusting.I used the level function in GIMP (free editing software)I am not saying it is perfect but IMO it looks better and would probably score more.', '2006-06-16 12:03:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522429, 344369, 25678, '<td valign="top">Hiya couchmate!  Nice job on this one!</td>', 'Hiya couchmate!  Nice job on this one!', '2006-06-16 12:22:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522430, 342398, 25678, '<td valign="top">Very nice!  Great lines and composition, and the water drops always add a little something nice.</td>', 'Very nice!  Great lines and composition, and the water drops always add a little something nice.', '2006-06-16 12:23:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522435, 342821, 42125, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2 Gunnsi<br/>First impression</b> <br/>I want to see her face!, The branches are in front of her eyes and that is very distracting. Either hide away the eye or show it all. In this way I get irritated looking at it and try to blink to get rid of the distraction. Good colours, green :-), good focus and lighting.<br/><b>What can you do better</b> <br/>Take away the little branches from her eye. :-)<br/>Good luck next time.</td>', 'Greetings from CTP2 GunnsiFirst impression I want to see her face!, The branches are in front of her eyes and that is very distracting. Either hide away the eye or show it all. In this way I get irritated looking at it and try to blink to get rid of the distraction. Good colours, green :-), good focus and lighting.What can you do better Take away the little branches from her eye. :-)Good luck next time.', '2006-06-16 12:25:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522471, 342246, 18655, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a top 10 finish - well deserved!</td>', 'Congrats on a top 10 finish - well deserved!', '2006-06-16 12:38:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522517, 344446, 42125, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2 Gunnsi<br/>First impression</b> <br/>Don''t know what to say! It screams at me. Can''t stop and look at any part of it, my eyes just wander to the next bit every time I try to stop. So in the end I stop where you didn''t want me to. Namely in the overblown section. So I think "Overblown" in stead of thinking: "Hey this is cool"<br/><b>What can you do better</b> <br/>Higher shutter speed or lower aperture to get rid of the overblown part.<br/>Also consider a different placement or add another thing beside it.</td>', 'Greetings from CTP2 GunnsiFirst impression Don''t know what to say! It screams at me. Can''t stop and look at any part of it, my eyes just wander to the next bit every time I try to stop. So in the end I stop where you didn''t want me to. Namely in the overblown section. So I think "Overblown" in stead of thinking: "Hey this is cool"What can you do better Higher shutter speed or lower aperture to get rid of the overblown part.Also consider a different placement or add another thing beside it.', '2006-06-16 13:04:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522598, 341054, 30454, '<td valign="top">WTG Leroy. Congratulations on your PB as in "Person Best" not "Peanut Butter". :o) I really like the simplicity and lighting.</td>', 'WTG Leroy. Congratulations on your PB as in "Person Best" not "Peanut Butter". :o) I really like the simplicity and lighting.', '2006-06-16 13:57:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522640, 342821, 30454, '<td valign="top">Greetings from your own critique club. Sorry, I was off the hook for a while.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression</b> <br/>Nice shot, may not meeting the challenge. Particularly there are so many DNMC police around in DPC. LOL <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Did not like tree in the forgraound. OOF foreground tree is still fine, but don''t like the focused branched on the face.<br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>There is lots green in picture, but the sunlight on the face with high contrast leads eye there.<br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Good DOF, colors. I think there is too much light on face compare to foreground and BG.<br/><b>Improvement:</b> <br/>Less light on face, more light on the green trees.<br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Not one of your best shot, I firmly believe you can do better than this.<br/> <br/>Cheers!! Keep shooting.</td>', 'Greetings from your own critique club. Sorry, I was off the hook for a while. First Impression Nice shot, may not meeting the challenge. Particularly there are so many DNMC police around in DPC. LOL Composition: Did not like tree in the forgraound. OOF foreground tree is still fine, but don''t like the focused branched on the face.Subject: There is lots green in picture, but the sunlight on the face with high contrast leads eye there.Technical (Colour and light): Good DOF, colors. I think there is too much light on face compare to foreground and BG.Improvement: Less light on face, more light on the green trees.Summary: Not one of your best shot, I firmly believe you can do better than this. Cheers!! Keep shooting.', '2006-06-16 14:21:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522694, 342250, 30454, '<td valign="top">Greetings from your own critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression</b> <br/>Very Nice shot with WOW factor. <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Perfect.<br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Very nice, perfect for the challenge.<br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Very nice ligting. Just wondering how it will look with more color saturation, particularly the green color. <br/><b>Improvement:</b> <br/>More saturation for green color.<br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Nice image with WOW factor. Nice composition, lighting and focus is spot on.<br/> <br/>Congratulations. Keep shooting.</td>', 'Greetings from your own critique club. First Impression Very Nice shot with WOW factor. Composition: Perfect.Subject: Very nice, perfect for the challenge.Technical (Colour and light): Very nice ligting. Just wondering how it will look with more color saturation, particularly the green color. Improvement: More saturation for green color.Summary: Nice image with WOW factor. Nice composition, lighting and focus is spot on. Congratulations. Keep shooting.', '2006-06-16 14:45:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522773, 344412, 368, '<td valign="top">great great photo ... i love it!!!</td>', 'great great photo ... i love it!!!', '2006-06-16 15:23:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522779, 343734, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - <br/> <br/>I gave this shot a 6 but may have been on the edge of giving it a 7 now that I look at it again. I like the concept and the overall capture. I think what takes away from it for me at least is the hue of the green stuff. I realize that it is probably pretty true to real life but I think a slightly more green/less yellow may have made this a bit easier on the eyes. With basic editing this may have been tough with trying to keep the gator a good shade. Nice sharpness on hte face and the background/foreground blur work well. The camouflage aspect makes you stick around a bit longer than most pics just to figure out all that is there. A good shot overall especially under basic editing restrictions. Tough to leave the string of 6s behind though - I can totally relate.</td>', 'Trading Post -  I gave this shot a 6 but may have been on the edge of giving it a 7 now that I look at it again. I like the concept and the overall capture. I think what takes away from it for me at least is the hue of the green stuff. I realize that it is probably pretty true to real life but I think a slightly more green/less yellow may have made this a bit easier on the eyes. With basic editing this may have been tough with trying to keep the gator a good shade. Nice sharpness on hte face and the background/foreground blur work well. The camouflage aspect makes you stick around a bit longer than most pics just to figure out all that is there. A good shot overall especially under basic editing restrictions. Tough to leave the string of 6s behind though - I can totally relate.', '2006-06-16 15:25:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522796, 344407, 30454, '<td valign="top">Nice one Judy. Good lighting and sharp focus. Continue great with the great scores..WPL2 is just around the corner.</td>', 'Nice one Judy. Good lighting and sharp focus. Continue great with the great scores..WPL2 is just around the corner.', '2006-06-16 15:34:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522804, 344412, 26513, '<td valign="top">This is one of the best pieces ive seen on here! awesome!</td>', 'This is one of the best pieces ive seen on here! awesome!', '2006-06-16 15:40:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522805, 341348, 53147, '<td valign="top">Tradin gPost -<br/> <br/>Overll a good capture. I have never tried taking bug shots so I have no clue what its like but I would think that these kind of shots can be tough. I think you got a pretty good shot considering the really high ISO setting. Good focus and detail on the bug. Not too much distracting noise going on. The colors are a bit oversaturated in my opinion. Like several of us inthe trading group - if this were advanced editing I think we all would have done much better. This fit the challenge but the colors are just a bit too much overprocessed. Congrats though on getting a top 3 profile pic. It is always nice to see a new pic in your highest rated profile. Keep it up.</td>', 'Tradin gPost - Overll a good capture. I have never tried taking bug shots so I have no clue what its like but I would think that these kind of shots can be tough. I think you got a pretty good shot considering the really high ISO setting. Good focus and detail on the bug. Not too much distracting noise going on. The colors are a bit oversaturated in my opinion. Like several of us inthe trading group - if this were advanced editing I think we all would have done much better. This fit the challenge but the colors are just a bit too much overprocessed. Congrats though on getting a top 3 profile pic. It is always nice to see a new pic in your highest rated profile. Keep it up.', '2006-06-16 15:42:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522820, 344412, 59029, '<td valign="top">Har har har!  How''d the hell I miss this one when voting?  It''s great!</td>', 'Har har har!  How''d the hell I miss this one when voting?  It''s great!', '2006-06-16 16:02:57.000000', NULL, 0),
