(2542974, 342512, 37893, '<td valign="top">Great take on the challenge and a new PB! This is a wonderful image that speaks of nature and her intricacies. Great use of DOF as well.</td>', 'Great take on the challenge and a new PB! This is a wonderful image that speaks of nature and her intricacies. Great use of DOF as well.', '2006-06-22 22:48:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2543952, 342821, 41337, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2</b> <br/> <br/>Ok, the two issues I have with this is the out of focus areas and those rouge branches over the face. In the out of focus areas I feel the blur doesn''t look good. When I look at that it looks like there are brush strokes probably just the way the blur was rendered but I would blur it more in post just so it was smoother. <br/> <br/>The other thing is the two branches over the face. I just wish they weren''t there. Other than that I like the image. The composition works great.</td>', 'Greetings from CTP2  Ok, the two issues I have with this is the out of focus areas and those rouge branches over the face. In the out of focus areas I feel the blur doesn''t look good. When I look at that it looks like there are brush strokes probably just the way the blur was rendered but I would blur it more in post just so it was smoother.  The other thing is the two branches over the face. I just wish they weren''t there. Other than that I like the image. The composition works great.', '2006-06-23 04:31:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2544064, 344361, 41337, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>This is unique and somehow you made something not interesting, interesting so good job there. The composition really kicks butt, IMO. <br/> <br/>However, since the masses didn''t agree I must now find lots of faults with this. :P Ok, you already know about the sky/background so skipping that I think having the girl in focus would have really helped a lot. Also, catching the horse''s mouth open would have helped hammer home that this horse is indeed eating! I don''t know why but voters I''m learning are like little children who need to be handheld every step of the way. I think you did a great job of that with your Take Two entry.<br/> <br/>So in summary, have a better sky/background, girl in focus and some eating action and I think your score would have improved by a good margin.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-23 04:30:49.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   This is unique and somehow you made something not interesting, interesting so good job there. The composition really kicks butt, IMO.  However, since the masses didn''t agree I must now find lots of faults with this. :P Ok, you already know about the sky/background so skipping that I think having the girl in focus would have really helped a lot. Also, catching the horse''s mouth open would have helped hammer home that this horse is indeed eating! I don''t know why but voters I''m learning are like little children who need to be handheld every step of the way. I think you did a great job of that with your Take Two entry. So in summary, have a better sky/background, girl in focus and some eating action and I think your score would have improved by a good margin.', '2006-06-23 05:29:01.000000', '2006-06-23 05:30:49.000000', 0),
(2546751, 342079, 16912, '<td valign="top">comment from my <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=336521&amp;page=1" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">1-4-0</a>  thread<br/> <br/>Hi Cyler, This isn''t a striking image for me though fits the challenge of green and does lead you nicely into (and out of) the image. You and others have mentioned the sky so I won''t, however, the other bit that bothers me is that the front post is not as sharp as I''d have liked. Forget the challenge and maybe revisit the area with a better sky and clone out the pilon wires and those three sticky up things.</td>', 'comment from my 1-4-0  thread Hi Cyler, This isn''t a striking image for me though fits the challenge of green and does lead you nicely into (and out of) the image. You and others have mentioned the sky so I won''t, however, the other bit that bothers me is that the front post is not as sharp as I''d have liked. Forget the challenge and maybe revisit the area with a better sky and clone out the pilon wires and those three sticky up things.', '2006-06-23 21:26:23.000000', NULL, 0),
