(2570327, 344361, 38496, '<td valign="top">I like the perspective on this one, and I like the girl in soft focus.  What I didn''t care for so much when I was voting, is that the title made me wonder what the brown stuff at the very front of the photo was... looks like something I don''t even what to think about the horse eating (ok, maybe I have too fertile of an imagination).  Also, the sky is sort of flat and dull in this shot - not that you can control the wheather Ü</td>', 'I like the perspective on this one, and I like the girl in soft focus.  What I didn''t care for so much when I was voting, is that the title made me wonder what the brown stuff at the very front of the photo was... looks like something I don''t even what to think about the horse eating (ok, maybe I have too fertile of an imagination).  Also, the sky is sort of flat and dull in this shot - not that you can control the wheather Ü', '2006-06-30 18:28:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2574298, 342960, 37858, '<td valign="top">As soon as I saw this topic I thought to myself, the Kermit pictures will be all over this one.  I was out of town I didn''t vote, so I don''t know if there were others.  It meets the challenge, but kermit (like yellow ducks and woodies) is pretty predictable.  That said, the idea is pretty clever and you have executed it well.  The technical aspect is fine.  I would have scored this a 5 or 6.  I suspect Kermit''s star power helped with the ratings because 28 scores at 9 or 10 seems high to me based purely on photographic merits (IMHO).  <br/> <br/>Since my own scores are pretty mediocre, maybe I''ll incorporate Kermit, duckie and woodie in my next picture to see if it makes a difference. ;-)</td>', 'As soon as I saw this topic I thought to myself, the Kermit pictures will be all over this one.  I was out of town I didn''t vote, so I don''t know if there were others.  It meets the challenge, but kermit (like yellow ducks and woodies) is pretty predictable.  That said, the idea is pretty clever and you have executed it well.  The technical aspect is fine.  I would have scored this a 5 or 6.  I suspect Kermit''s star power helped with the ratings because 28 scores at 9 or 10 seems high to me based purely on photographic merits (IMHO).   Since my own scores are pretty mediocre, maybe I''ll incorporate Kermit, duckie and woodie in my next picture to see if it makes a difference. ;-)', '2006-07-02 08:05:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2574358, 344490, 37858, '<td valign="top">Trading Post<br/> <br/>I like the simplicity of this shot and the bokeh.  The textures are good, but the light is a bit flat IMHO.  I was out of town and didn''t vote on this one.  I probably would have gone with a 5 or 6.</td>', 'Trading Post I like the simplicity of this shot and the bokeh.  The textures are good, but the light is a bit flat IMHO.  I was out of town and didn''t vote on this one.  I probably would have gone with a 5 or 6.', '2006-07-02 08:59:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2574363, 343734, 37858, '<td valign="top">Trading Post<br/> <br/>Interesting photo.  I see you used a zoom lens.  I hope you were on the 200mm end of that one given the subject.  This certainly meets the Green requirement of the challenge.  The murkiness of the water is a bit distracting...like having too noisy or grainy a picture.  I was out of town and couldn''t vote, but would have probably put this down as a 6.</td>', 'Trading Post Interesting photo.  I see you used a zoom lens.  I hope you were on the 200mm end of that one given the subject.  This certainly meets the Green requirement of the challenge.  The murkiness of the water is a bit distracting...like having too noisy or grainy a picture.  I was out of town and couldn''t vote, but would have probably put this down as a 6.', '2006-07-02 09:03:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2574395, 341348, 37858, '<td valign="top">Trading Post<br/> <br/>One of your better efforts IMHO.  Meets the challenge well.  Good focus.  Technically fine.  Lighting good.  Nothing I can think of to improve this.  I was out of town and couldn''t vote, but I would have scored this at least a 7.</td>', 'Trading Post One of your better efforts IMHO.  Meets the challenge well.  Good focus.  Technically fine.  Lighting good.  Nothing I can think of to improve this.  I was out of town and couldn''t vote, but I would have scored this at least a 7.', '2006-07-02 09:39:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2574737, 344433, 18339, '<td valign="top">eewwww!  Nice capture though :p</td>', 'eewwww!  Nice capture though :p', '2006-07-02 12:58:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2575019, 341482, 41337, '<td valign="top">Wonderful lighting and color. What a fitting shot for the challenge! I didn''t vote in this challenge but if I did, I couldn''t see myself giving anything lower than a 7. <br/> <br/>That flowing hair and her expression makes me wonder how this would look in another crop. I know this was entered for the green challenge and the crop you used works well for that purpose but I''m wondering if a much tighter crop would help convey your daughter''s expression and personality better. For example, when I pull this in photoshop I cut off a bit from the top so part of her hat is missing and from the bottom I cut off up to where her hair ends. It''s a little more square like, but for me anyway, it adds something that compliments the way she is posing. If I had more to work with on the left side I might also think about going with a more landscape look with the crop example I gave. <br/> <br/>Anyway just some random thoughts. This is very good and I could only wish to produce professional looking images like this. Good luck in future challenges!</td>', 'Wonderful lighting and color. What a fitting shot for the challenge! I didn''t vote in this challenge but if I did, I couldn''t see myself giving anything lower than a 7.  That flowing hair and her expression makes me wonder how this would look in another crop. I know this was entered for the green challenge and the crop you used works well for that purpose but I''m wondering if a much tighter crop would help convey your daughter''s expression and personality better. For example, when I pull this in photoshop I cut off a bit from the top so part of her hat is missing and from the bottom I cut off up to where her hair ends. It''s a little more square like, but for me anyway, it adds something that compliments the way she is posing. If I had more to work with on the left side I might also think about going with a more landscape look with the crop example I gave.  Anyway just some random thoughts. This is very good and I could only wish to produce professional looking images like this. Good luck in future challenges!', '2006-07-02 16:18:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2576218, 342400, 60223, '<td valign="top">Wow, those two large droplets look like jewels, they really stand out.  In your notes you state you adjusted brightness and contrast, I think less brightness would have added some depth to the picture.  Also, having the leaves in the top left sticking into the frame and having them closer than your subject and out of focus doesn''t work here.</td>', 'Wow, those two large droplets look like jewels, they really stand out.  In your notes you state you adjusted brightness and contrast, I think less brightness would have added some depth to the picture.  Also, having the leaves in the top left sticking into the frame and having them closer than your subject and out of focus doesn''t work here.', '2006-07-03 00:46:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2578224, 343734, 14620, '<td valign="top">Ha, just saw this.  I almost submitted the exact same shot for this challenge but it wasn''t quite as good as this one.  Funny thing is that we saw him a couple hours or so after you guys did and he was still doing the same thing probably in the exact same place. :-)</td>', 'Ha, just saw this.  I almost submitted the exact same shot for this challenge but it wasn''t quite as good as this one.  Funny thing is that we saw him a couple hours or so after you guys did and he was still doing the same thing probably in the exact same place. :-)', '2006-07-03 09:50:19.000000', NULL, 0),
